export anchor FieldGuideStyle:
    number: 130
    screen: ProjectsDashboard
    name: Field guide
    idea: The dashboard as a pocket naturalist's guide, with thumb index tabs for navigation, each project written up as a species account with a plate drawing, field marks and a range map to its due date, and the chart drawn as a seasonal abundance band.
    base: light
    palette:
        desk: #dcd8c6, behind the book
        page: #faf7ee, the guide's pages
        ink: #232a22, text, line drawings and rules
        pencil: #55594d, captions, times and map labels
        rule: #cfc8b0, thin rules between accounts, never text
        moss: #3c6b3f, the primary button and the kicker
        rangeOchre: #c99a3c, range map shading on #ebe6d3
        abundance: #5d7f4c, last week in the band, with #2f5d73 for this week
        plateWashes: #f0d9b5 design, #cfdcea engineering, #d6e6c9 research, #ecd0cf marketing
        onTrack: #2c6a33, the dot
        atRisk: #8a4f00, the triangle
        behind: #9b2f2a, the diamond and overdue
    type:
        Names and labels use Franklin Gothic Medium, Franklin Gothic, ITC
        Franklin Gothic, Arial Narrow, Arial, sans-serif. Text uses Iowan Old
        Style, Charter, Bitstream Charter, Georgia, serif. The greeting is
        42px 700 sans at 1.08, section titles 22px 700 sans, species names
        19px 700 sans, team lines 16px italic serif, body 15 to 16px serif
        at 1.5, run-in labels such as Field marks in bold sans, times 12.5px
        caps sans.
    layout:
        A book spread up to 1240px on the desk colour, its fore edge rounded
        14px with stacked page edges below, and six coloured thumb index tabs
        standing off the right edge with vertical labels, the current Home
        tab wider with a heavy outline. A ruled running head has a round bird
        mark, the brand with A field guide to the team's projects, a search,
        a moss New project button, a square bell and the avatar with the
        name. The intro has the kicker Today in the field, the greeting, the
        italic date and a pink bar with a diamond saying Look out first for
        4 tasks that are overdue, beside a boxed Quick identification key
        with four small pictures and the numbers. Species accounts fill two
        thirds in two columns. Each account has a round wash plate with a
        line drawing for the team, a pen nib, a gear, a magnifier or a
        megaphone, and a black plate number, then the name, the team in
        italic, Field marks with percent and tasks, Status, and Range from
        now to the due date over a small Nov Dec Jan map shaded up to a dot
        on the due date. Recent sightings fills the last third. Seasonal
        abundance draws the 14 days as one horizontal band whose thickness
        follows each value, green then blue, with values, day letters and
        dates. Below 900px the tabs become a row of tabs under the header
        and everything stacks.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 16px between accounts, 32 to 40px between columns and 24px section padding.
    density: Bookish and fairly dense. Two columns of accounts beside a sightings column.
    corners: 3px on controls, round plates and avatars, and the book rounds 14px on its fore edge.
    borders: 1px ink under the running head, 1px pale rules between accounts and one boxed key.
    shadows: Stacked page edges under the spread and one soft drop. Accounts have none.
    icons:
        Hand drawn line pictures at 2.4 stroke on soft round washes, and
        tiny solid status marks at 14px with the word, a dot for On track, a
        triangle for At risk and a diamond for Behind.
    focus: A 3px slate blue outline offset 2px.
    tone: Naturalist's notes, such as Field marks, Range, Look out first for and Recent sightings.
